10 different conditions for class "1" (Has postpartum depression):  
- Need for Support is Low  
- Fear of pregnancy is Yes  
- Relationship with the in-laws is in [Bad, Poor]  
- Occupation before latest pregnancy is in [Housewife, Student, Other]  
- Age of newborn is in [0 to 6 months, 1 year to 1.5 year]  
- Pregnancy plan is No or Yes (both appear, but mostly Yes with other risk factors)  
- Residence is in [City, Village] (no strong pattern, but often City)  
- Monthly income before latest pregnancy is No or More than 30000 (both extremes)  
- Mode of delivery is Normal Delivery or Caesarean Section with Fear of pregnancy Yes  
- Pregnancy length is in [8 months, 9 months, 10 months] with other risk factors  

---

Summary:  
Class 0 (No postpartum depression) is associated with medium or no need for support, no fear, good/neutral relationships, planned pregnancy, older baby, city residence, and moderate to high income.  
Class 1 (Postpartum depression) is associated with low need for support (possibly indicating unexpressed needs), fear of pregnancy, bad relationships, housewife/student occupation, younger baby, unplanned or planned pregnancy but with other risk factors, and extremes of income.

